                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The government warns that adopting the respondent\u2019s interpretation would have harmful consequences for the ACCA and other important federal statutes."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Government)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Kannon K. Shanmugam (Petitioner)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5564e048b47ed164e40c24bf64812da3f87f7fb081171eeed2c5850164d16c12",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5564e048b47e-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Kannon K. Shanmugam (Petitioner), according to Kannon K. Shanmugam (Petitioner), the respondent argues that the ACCA\u2019s language can accommodate alternative maximum terms for different tiers of offenders, such as recidivists and non\u2011recidivists."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Shanmugam",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5564e048b47ed164e40c24bf64812da3f87f7fb081171eeed2c5850164d16c12",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5564e048b47e-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Shanmugam, the respondent maintains that the statute speaks of a maximum term for the offense, not the offender, allowing distinct maxima for repeat versus first\u2011time offenders, but not individualized maxima for each offender."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Shanmugam",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5564e048b47ed164e40c24bf64812da3f87f7fb081171eeed2c5850164d16c12",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5564e048b47e-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Shanmugam, if the Court adopts an interpretation requiring a single maximum, then all offenders of offenses with a possible ten\u2011year sentence would be subject to the ACCA."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5564e048b47ed164e40c24bf64812da3f87f7fb081171eeed2c5850164d16c12",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5564e048b47e-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, congress intended the ACCA to target serious offenses based on what defendants actually did, not a generic three\u2011strikes rule."
        }
